{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"7462a1246f8f146da48b0b696fd9cc23e80845ad36758c8a930abde2d6677609","slug":"structured-populations","location":"/Discrete_Models/Structured_Populations.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Structured Populations","content_includes_title":false,"keywords":["math-models","biological context"],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"Structured_Populations.md","url":"/Structured_Populatio-d9753fad663391eed04e3e2d96bf4bef.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Introduction","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"CA09s0Oi7c"}],"identifier":"introduction","label":"Introduction","html_id":"introduction","implicit":true,"key":"hrkvaLJabM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So far in our models, all individuals in a population were treated identically. Although our exponential model may work for ''simple\" organisms such as single-celled bacteria or protozoa, in most populations, there are actually many subgroups whose vital behaviour can be quite different.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"eakpQbtxPS"}],"key":"RukhXfVJkO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Therefore, we extend our discrete models to a population divided into different subgroups whose reproduction and mortality rates depend on and influence each other.  For example, we could have an age-structured population, where reproduction only occurs after the individual has matured, while death rates are higher for either for newly-borns and/or for the oldest in the population who are more vulnerable to predators, parasite, and disease. Or, we could also have a stage-structured population, as for many insects which pass through the egg, larval, pupal, and adult stages and survival is influenced by which phase they are in. These are called ","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"o1pgzwK3R8"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"structured populations","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"Ch44LUApBH"}],"key":"PSvhXyTGlg"}],"key":"ewJzlHyqtJ"},{"type":"text","value":". We will focus on linear models and develop a ","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"ZFKEDNEOFU"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"system of equations","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"DQYOjG0TBP"}],"key":"odAlBfMMXf"}],"key":"C1Xs8LDYo0"},{"type":"text","value":" (with a different growth equation for each subgroup), and use ","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"WqBQ0lio2G"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"matrices","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"SB8igNoQ7q"}],"key":"K1Nj20MCod"}],"key":"qxpfm2vM0G"},{"type":"text","value":" to solve them.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"k06L4eH7e9"}],"key":"qau9JMdYQF"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line